    "body": "<!-- pr-reviewer: 4a5c9dd4ca304735f31ce9f936c4e66cecda0c26 -->\n**Ready for the maintainer to merge** (high tier, inline; P0 build break #844).\n\nChecked against upstream/main (MERGEABLE, 3 files in camcraft-motion):\n- **trochoid_slot.rs:** `measure()`'s new `Result` goes through a `gauge` closure that maps to a named `GenError::Invalid(\"trochoidal slot: measuring stock: ...\")`, and both call sites propagate with `?`.\n- **trochoid_air.rs:** `lifted_cut` now takes `&mut Stock` and returns `Result<Option<Point3>, StockError>`. Both `columns()?` and `subtract_flat(..)?` propagate, and the caller maps an `Err` to a named refusal (\"reading the lifted returns\"), so an unreadable stock is never a pass. `Columns::col` returns `None` off the lattice, as `Dexel::col` did, so the law reads as before.\n- **origin_approach:** `PathBuilder::approached` adds a leading rapid only when the first move isn't a rapid. `finish()`'s first push is a rapid, so the path is byte-unchanged.\n- **Tests:** they now match on `Ok(None)` and `Ok(Some(_))`, so the caught-return pin still requires a hit.\n\nRun locally on 4a5c9dd4 (private target): `camcraft-motion --test trochoid_slot` 10 passed, `--test origin_approach` 5 passed, `clippy -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -D warnings` clean. No goldens, process files or dependencies touched.",
